---
import { caseSources } from '../data/research';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/nav';

const sources = caseSources;
---

<Base title="About — The Courtyard Block" current="about">
  <header class="mx-auto max-w-[920px] px-6 pt-20 sm:px-12">
    <p class="mb-4 font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-terracotta">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(40px,5.5vw,68px)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.015em]">
      A hopeful idea. With footnotes.
    </h1>
  </header>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p class="text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      This site came out of a conversation about wanting to live in a place that is both a
      food-forest eco-village <em>and</em> a Berlin-like city — two dreams that seem opposed until
      you notice one building holding both: gardens, shared rooms, and children underfoot in the
      middle; trams, strangers, and a bakery at the edge. The resolution is not a compound in the
      countryside. It is one mid-rise courtyard building in a real city. Then another.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-[920px] px-6 sm:px-12">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[30px] font-medium">Sources</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 max-w-[65ch] text-lg leading-[1.6] text-ink/85">
      The atlas prioritizes project, architect, cooperative and city publications. Those sources describe built features and intended design; they do not independently establish resident happiness, whole-life cost or environmental performance. Each case separates the project record from our questions for another place. The Berkeley and city pages are exploratory briefs, not legal or investment advice.
    </p>
    <p class="research-note mb-6">October 2026 review: corrected the combined Sargfabrik/Miss Sargfabrik dates and counts; separated public and resident facilities at Gleis 21; clarified Swan’s Market’s multiple delivery arrangements. Removed unsourced savings, legal-reform counts and universal climate or community guarantees. Corrections improve the invitation, not diminish it.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,320px),1fr))] gap-x-10">
      {
        sources.map((s) => (
          <div class="border-b border-ink/15 py-4">
            <span class="text-[17px]">{s.name}</span>
            <a
              href={s.url}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="mt-1 block font-sans text-sm text-terracotta"
            >
              {s.label} ↗
            </a>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-[920px] px-6 sm:px-12">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[30px] font-medium">Credits &amp; license</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[65ch] text-lg leading-[1.6] text-ink/85">
      Original text and diagrams on this site are offered under <strong>CC BY-NC 4.0</strong> — copy
      the brief, redraw the sections, start one in your city. Photographs keep their own licenses
      and credits; see
      <a href="https://github.com/crs48/courtyard-block-site/blob/main/IMAGE-CREDITS.md"
        ><em>IMAGE-CREDITS</em></a
      > in the <a href="https://github.com/crs48/courtyard-block-site">repository</a>. Every speculative
      drawing is labeled illustrative.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[65ch] text-lg leading-[1.6] text-ink/85">
      Corrections are welcome and wanted — especially from residents of the buildings in the atlas.
      If a fact is wrong,
      <a href="https://github.com/crs48/courtyard-block-site/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a> so it can be reviewed and corrected with a note.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-22 max-w-[1240px] px-6 sm:px-12">
    <a href={withBase('/how/')} class="block border-2 border-ink bg-paper-raised px-12 py-11 no-underline">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-terracotta">Join</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[clamp(26px,3vw,38px)] font-medium leading-[1.2]">
        If you would live in this building, help write it →
      </p>
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>
